Human valk in my current game, getting mixed messages from the RNG. 
Which usually means my current toon's doomed.

Found an early pair of speed boots and an early suit of +4(!) splint 
mail. Found a second-hand bookstore and price-ID'd ?oID. Lost my dog 
to a rock trap on or near the Oracle level (RIP) and didn't have the 
means to tame another pet (Boo!). Oracle contained bones with some 
interesting loot: T-shirt (altar-check in Minetown would reveal this 
as cursed), tinning kit (also cursed), magic marker (cursed), and 
some other things I don't remember offhand (not logged in to the 
account with that save). Dipping into the fountains yielded 
Excalibur, and only dried up one other fountain in the process.

Sokoban brought in more loot, including various wands (speed monster, 
sleep, magic missile) and so much food I became burdened just 
carrying it all. Thankfully I got the bag from the zoo, picking up PR 
from a helpful shrieker along the way. A couple PEBKACs beforehand 
made this harder than it should have, including blocking one boulder 
against another; had to drop my stuff and squeeze past to unblock it. 
At least I only took that one luck hit.

Got expert dagger somewhere in there, and now wielding (currently 
skilled) Excalibur.

Dive to Minetown was relatively uneventful, and I finally curse-
tested my inventory at the coaligned temple. One of those ID scrolls 
was blessed (Yay!). Only got 4 items out of it, though (=oWarning, 
=oSR, +2=oGCon, =oLev). Put on warning and gain con, which helped 
with the burdened inventory. Also sacced for Mojo; it's currently in 
the bag. Thinking of raising it to skilled after upping twoweapon.

Two levelporters made the dive to Mine's End aggravating (back to 
DL1? Really?!) but I eventually liberated the luckstone. Around this 
point I'm thinking, "All this stuff to use holy water on... and only 
one thing of water. You're killing me, game." Which means the RNG's 
doing its job at least passably.

Ended up stressed somewhere along the way, even with most of my 
unused stuff in the bag. Later narrowed it down to a pile of food 
rations. Took some clever thinking to get all my stuff out of the 
Mines. Considering stashing those rations, given my next discovery.

Upon exiting the mines, I noticed that I had two bronze rings, one of 
them cursed, and a sink on the level. Stash a bunch of (mostly 
uninteresting) stuff in a large box I brought near the Mines 
downstair and head for the sink. On the way, "Valkyrie needs food, 
badly!" Oops. I dispatch the nearby dwarf (who was generated hostile 
for some reason) and pray for food. Stupid; should've eaten a ration, 
I got plenty to burn. I get to the sink and drop the cursed ring in 
-- "The ring is regurgitated!" Well, won't need those rations for 
some time.

Right now, I'm making my way back down while waiting for that /oDeath 
to show up in an intelligent monster's hands. Especially given that I 
haven't encountered reflection or MR yet.


